about=heading('01','ABOUT','A curiosity that<br>became a direction.','Christopher Horne · Student meteorologist · UNC Charlotte')+'''<section class="section story-grid"><aside class="profile-mark"><img src="../assets/ch-weather-logo.png" width="300" height="300" alt="CH Weather logo"><p class="eyebrow">CHRISTOPHER HORNE</p><p>B.S. Meteorology<br>Mathematics minor<br>Expected Spring 2028</p></aside><div class="prose"><h2>It started with a snow day.</h2><p>I’ve been fascinated by weather since fifth grade, when nine inches of snow fell on my birthday in Charlotte. Since then, I’ve seen a tornado and experienced hurricanes at the beach, including Hurricane Matthew.</p><p>Seeing how severe weather affected my family gave that interest a purpose: helping people understand what is happening, what remains uncertain, and what they can do to prepare.</p><h2>Science with people in mind.</h2><p>I’m pursuing a B.S. in Meteorology with a minor in Mathematics at UNC Charlotte, with an expected graduation in spring 2028. My interests span operational forecasting, weather intelligence, risk management, and public communication.</p><p>Through CH Weather, I’m developing a place to explain Carolina weather in everyday language while keeping the science and uncertainty clear.</p><h2>Beyond the classroom.</h2><p>I enjoy storm chasing, photography, and music. I’d love to connect with others who share those interests. My more than four years at Chick-fil-A, including work as a team leader, have also shaped how I communicate and work with people.</p><a class="text-link" href="contact.html">Let’s connect <span>↗</span></a></div></section>'''

